= Questions and answers <faq>

== "I don't see a part I need."
#who("member")

Musicus shows you a part when one of your groups may read its instrument or
its whole score. Ask your librarian or admin to check:

+ Are you in the right group? (#ui("Groups"), admins change the members)
+ May this group read the part's instrument? (same page, *Instruments*)
+ Is the part tagged with the right instrument, and does it have a file?
  (in the #ui("Library"), #ui("Edit") under the part)

Changes apply immediately; reload the library page.

== "I was logged out."

This happens when you did not use Musicus on this device for longer than
60 days, when you changed your password on another device, or when an admin
logged you out. Simply log in again. Your markings are not affected.

If you forgot your password, ask an admin for a new link (@users).

== "I can't stay logged in on my tablet."
#who("admin")

The tablet probably uses an address with plain `http://`. Browsers only keep
logins for secure connections; set up HTTPS (@https).

== "Can the admin or the librarian see my markings?"

No. Markings are only shown to the person who made them. Admins can neither
see nor change them through Musicus.

== "What if the Wi-Fi fails during the concert?"

Every piece of a programme you opened beforehand (with the green "ready"
message) keeps working, as long as the browser tab stays open. Markings you
make while offline cannot be saved until the connection is back; leave the
reader open until the status shows *Saved*.

== "What happens to my markings when I close the browser?"

They are saved on the server and come back on your next visit, on any
device. Only the downloaded sheets are gone and are downloaded again the
next time.

== "Someone left the ensemble."
#who("admin")

Click #ui("Disable") next to the account (#ui("Users")). The
person is logged out everywhere at once and cannot log in any more.

== "Which browsers work?"

Current versions of Safari (iPad, iPhone, Mac), Chrome, Edge and Firefox.
For the screen-keeps-on function and reliable logins, use HTTPS.
